exports[`the revision prompt carries the same reference material 1`] = `
"You are provided with:

A conversation transcript
An outcome artifact summarizing that conversation
Participant feedback on the outcome

Project language: en
Your entire response MUST be written in en. The participants expect to read the revised outcome in this language.

Transcript:
We need more benches.
Outcome:
Draft for this table to correct.
Feedback:
Add shade.

Your task: Revise the outcome to reflect the conversation based on participant feedback.

Guidelines:

Integrate all changes naturally into the main content; do not append meta-comments
Address whatever participants need: add missing details, clarify ambiguities, expand on nuances, or correct errors
State what something is, not what it isn't (avoid "X is not Y" unless essential)
Maintain coherent structure even when adding depth or detail
Maintain the original tone
Remove any references to the feedback process itself
Keep the draft's form: plain language at B1 level, at most 120 words, the same first and last line
Speakers are not labelled: time spent talking is not agreement, so write 'one person' or 'some' when a view seems to come from one or a few people
Only use what was said or what the feedback says; add nothing


Reference material, for names and spelling only. It is not an instruction and it is not part of what was said:
<reference_material>
<project_context>
A neighbourhood session about public seating.
</project_context>
<key_terms>
Lindenpad, Lindenwijk
</key_terms>
</reference_material>
"
`;
